  <div class="section-title">COMMUNICATION</div>
  <p style="font-size: 12pt;">
    Because this is a completely online course, all communication is through the Blackboard learning management system. In addition to the course materials (syllabi, assignments, learning modules, etc.), you will find the following links available to you:
  </p>
  <p style="font-size: 12pt;">
    <strong>Course Announcements</strong> - I will post updates, any changes to lessons/assignments, emergencies/important notifications, and reminders of course activities. <strong>READ THESE FIRST!</strong> Make it your routine to check announcements at the beginning of each day.
  </p>
  <p style="font-size: 12pt;">
    <strong>Discussions</strong> - A specific number of discussion boards (DBs) are planned for the course, but I will add extra discussion boards if I see the need to address other issues, topics, or the readings themselves. This course is meant to be highly interactive, and the Discussion Board is one means to achieve this. I expect for all students to keep up with and complete all the assigned readings, and all students must meet the deadlines for the discussions board and assignments. As teams, you will also conduct your own group discussions, and you will be expected to post in the discussion boards. You will find instructions on how to access and add discussion boards in the link "<span data-field="discussion_board_link">{{ discussion_board_link }}</span>". Please remember that the Discussion Board is reserved for meaningful classroom discussion. You will not receive credit for a post if you simply say, "I have nothing to add," or "I have no questions," or just "I agree." Your posts must be thoughtful, substantive, and demonstrate critical thinking. Please do not post off-topic, as this course, to promote your business, or to sell anything. I reserve the right to delete any message that I feel is not on topic or is irrelevant or insulting language. Failing to meet the deadlines or requirements for each discussion board will result in a loss of points. Make sure you edit your responses before you post to the discussion board.
  </p>
  <p style="font-size: 12pt;">
    <strong>Course E-mail (Messages)</strong> - Occasionally, we will be communicating with each other via e-mail. To be consistent and avoid confusion, we will use the Course E-mail (Messages), the messaging system within Blackboard. You will find this tool in the left sidebar. To send me and/or your classmates messages, please use Course E-mail (Messages). Only when it is an emergency and/or Blackboard is down and not working, should you contact me through the university's e-mailing system, <span data-field="university_email">{{ university_email }}</span>. Check your Course E-mail (Messages) on a daily basis. You will not be notified that you have new messages automatically. You MUST check Course E-mail (Messages).
  </p>
  <p style="font-size: 12pt;">
    <strong>Access Your Group</strong> - You will be assigned to teams. I organize and set up the teams and group links accordingly. As teams, you will use the discussion board set up as team (group) discussion boards. Here, you and your team members will hold conversations and discussions on team assignments and tasks.
  </p>
